# Portfolio — Core Architecture

Before any change: re-read this file and the glob-scoped rule that matches the files you touch.

## Architecture (non-negotiable)

- **Stack:** Next.js 14 App Router, TypeScript strict, Tailwind CSS, Framer Motion, next-themes.
- **Type:** Space Grotesk (headings / `font-display`) + DM Sans (body / `font-sans`) — Lovable reference pair.
- **Pattern:** Jamstack — static MDX content at build time; **one** dynamic path: `POST /api/contact`.
- **No:** database, auth, CMS, Docker, AI/LLM, queues, second animation library (no GSAP), external UI package (`@surajrao/my-ui-library` is out of scope — build primitives locally).
- **Layout:** `app/`, `components/`, `components/mdx/`, `components/motion/`, `lib/`, `content/`, `tests/`.
- **Rendering:** Server Components by default. `"use client"` only for interactivity, motion, theme toggle, or browser APIs.
- **UI:** Site-owned components only (`Button`, theme provider, cards, Hero, MDX renderers). Keep domain-independent primitives small and local under `components/ui/` when needed.

## Git workflow

1. Branch from up-to-date `develop`: `feature/<name>` or `chore/<name>`.
2. Conventional Commits only (`feat:`, `fix:`, `chore:`, `docs:`, `test:`, `ci:`).
3. Finish feature → **commit on branch → stop**. Human merges to `develop`. Do not merge unless asked.
4. Never commit `Portfolio_Site_Blueprint.md`, `TRACKER.md`, `.env*`, or secrets.
5. After each milestone: update local `TRACKER.md` (gitignored).

## Clean architecture principles

- **Dependencies point inward:** pages orchestrate; components present; `lib/` holds pure loaders, validation, and integrations.
- **Single responsibility** per module/file; meaningful names (`rate-limit.ts`, not `utils2.ts`).
- **No placeholders:** real implementations or don't ship the file. Ask if blocked on missing secrets/copy.
- **Scope discipline:** change only what the feature requires; no drive-by refactors.
- **Comments:** only when intent or constraint is non-obvious.

## Performance & a11y baseline

- Lazy-mount heavy client UI (`next/dynamic`, `{ ssr: false }` where needed): custom cursor, celestial background.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` everywhere animation exists.
- Semantic HTML landmarks; heading hierarchy; labels on form controls.
- Prefer transform/opacity for animation (compositor-friendly).

## Orchestration

- Parallelize features only when file sets do not overlap.
- Prefer small focused agents over one mega-change to save context.
- Prefer tools over long chat; implement, then brief milestone summary.
